course: dictionary
lesson: 2821
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A dictionary often gives one word more than one meaning. The word ditch is a good example. Read the sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits. «Mole ran off, crept back along a ditch and peeped through the hedge.» Here a ditch is a long, narrow hole in the ground beside a path, so Mole could creep along it and hide.
explain: The context tells you which meaning to pick. In «Keep away from storm drains, ditches and culverts, because fast water can sweep a child into a drain pipe», a ditch is a dug channel where water runs, and it can be dangerous. The words around it tell you that the water is the important part.
explain: Ditch can also be a verb, a doing word. To ditch something means to get rid of it or leave it, and this meaning is informal, so you would use it in friendly, chatty English. If the sentence is about a hole, ditch is a noun. If it is about getting rid of something, ditch is a verb.
fact: A ditch is a long, narrow hole dug in the ground, often along a road or field, to carry water away.
fact: In farming, ditches carry rainwater away from fields so the crops do not drown.
fact: To ditch something means to get rid of it or leave it; this meaning is informal.
fact: To ditch a plane means to land it on water in an emergency.
fact: A «last-ditch try» is a final try, made when everything else has failed.
exercise: «Mole ran off, crept back along a ditch and peeped through the hedge.» In this sentence, what is a ditch? | A kind of hat | *A long, narrow hole in the ground | A tall tree | A loud song
exercise: Max says, «I'm going to ditch my old trainers.» What does ditch mean here? | Land them on water | *Get rid of them | Wash them carefully | Dig a hole for them
exercise: «Keep away from storm drains, ditches and culverts.» Why should you keep away? | Ditches are warm, dry places to rest | Ditches are full of sweets | *Fast water can sweep a child into a drain pipe | Culverts are always empty, so they are safe
test: What does «a last-ditch try» mean? | A try that nobody watched | The first try of the day | A try made inside a ditch | *A final try, made when all else has failed
test: «The pilot had to ditch the plane on the lake.» What does ditch mean here? | Park it in a garage | *Land it on water in an emergency | Fly it very high | Dig a long hole for it
exam: Which sentence uses ditch as a verb, meaning to get rid of something? | *Sam wants to ditch the idea of a late bedtime | Mole crept along a ditch | The rain filled the ditch by the road | Keep away from the ditches
